    "features": "<p>Even in a time of relative peace, safety and enforcement are as important for the Union as any other organization. This includes patrolling stations, escorting individuals, or keeping watch of valuables. However, security on Medina Station is no different than elsewhere; guards and officers range from retired spacers looking for a steady wage to grizzled ex-OPA hired for their loyalty, violence, or willingness to take a bullet. High-ranking officers will sometimes hire crews for temporary security contracts, such as escorting precious cargo through a ring gate or placing ships in the slow zone under a mandatory security contract during a crisis. The statistics provided here can also be used for any generic security guard.</p><p><strong>Favored Stunts:</strong> Group Tactics, Restrain, Skirmish</p><p><strong>Talents:</strong> Protect (Novice), Tactical Awareness (Novice)</p><p><strong>Equipment:</strong> handcuffs, hand terminal, pistol, stun pistol, scanner, uniform</p><p><strong>Armor + Toughness:</strong> 1</p>",
    "statBlockView": true
